error[E1012]: region `r` is frozen, so it cannot be opened for mutation
 --> mem:///main.lu:4:13
  |
3 |     let f = freeze r
  |             -------- the freeze happens here — the promotion to `imm` is deep and permanent
4 |     let n = in f { 1 }
  |             ^^^^^^^^^^ `in` opens a region for writing
  |
  = note: `freeze` promotes the whole graph to `imm`: readable and shareable from anywhere,
    forever, and never writable again. Do the mutation before the freeze, or build a fresh
    region and `copy` what you need.
